2025/26 Evaluation Report","url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk/documents/s97576/annex-1-ukspf-programme-2025-26-evaluation-report.pdf","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","date":"25/06/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Housing and Planning Scrutiny Select Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Communities and Environment Scrutiny Select Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-17","committee":"Finance, Regeneration and Property Scrutiny Select Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-01","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Finance, Regeneration and Property Scrutiny Select Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Communities and Environment Scrutiny Select Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Tonbridge and Malling eliminates \u00a32.8m funding gap but LGR pause creates 2026-27 uncertainty","lead":"The council has eliminated a previously forecast \u00a32.8m funding gap and moved to a balanced budget for 2026-27, following a favourable government funding settlement and updated financial assumptions. The auditor confirmed the accounts are sound with no significant weaknesses. However, uncertainty has grown after government paused local government reorganisation decisions on 7 September. The council had been planning to merge with Maidstone, Sevenoaks and Tonbridge Wells into a West Kent unitary authority, but the vesting date is now uncertain. The auditor flagged the pause as creating heightened risks to financial stewardship during 2026-27.","iso":"2026-09-28","paper_title":"Annex 2 - Audit Findings Report","paper_url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk/documents/s100302/100302.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annex 1a - Strategic Risk Register","paper_url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk/documents/s100364/100364.pdf","headline":"Local Government Reorganisation deferral announced early September 2026; unitary council to begin March 2028, reducing immediate uncertainty but structural change confirmed","detail":"LGR will end Tonbridge and Malling in March 2028. Recent deferral announcement in early September 2026 has reduced immediate uncertainty. Risk of operational shortfall from staff departures persists. New unitary council may be burdened with historic county debt. Shared strategic partner being procured to support collaboration through Vesting Day April 2028. Close working at Leader and Chief Executive level. Risk score 16.","category":"governance","matters":"A lender needs to understand whether the council has leadership stability through 2028, whether debt obligations are being managed, and what structural changes will affect successor council creditworthiness","figures":"Vesting Day April 2028; LGR deferral announced early September 2026; risk score 16","quote":"Recent announcement on deferal of LGR in early September 2026 has resulted in longer term risk being reduced","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annex 1a - Strategic Risk Register","paper_url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk/documents/s100364/100364.pdf","headline":"Managed exit from Agile system and transition back to Uniform \u2014 new operational risk with data transfer and staffing implications","detail":"Council executing managed exit from Agile system with return to Uniform system. PID signed with IDOX establishing technical requirements for data return. Clear project plan with achievable milestones. Post-implementation review being carried out by internal audit with live lessons learned being implemented. Continued monitoring by implementation staff. Risk identified September 2026. Risk score 12.","category":"governance","matters":"A lender needs to know whether the council's planning and regulatory systems remain stable during this transition and whether there are risks to data integrity","figures":"Risk identified September 2026; risk score 12; PID signed with IDOX","quote":"Failure to deliver a managed exit from Agile and transition back to Uniform System","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annex 1a - Strategic Risk Register","paper_url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk/documents/s100364/100364.pdf","headline":"Staff recruitment and retention pressures addressed with 4% pay award agreed February 2026","detail":"Loss of capacity due to staff retirements (workforce age profile), staff departures to higher-paying roles, recruitment difficulties in key professional roles, and uncertainty from Local Government Reorganisation. Competition from private sector and London Boroughs. Council agreed 4% pay award in February 2026. Workforce Strategy reviewed June 2026. Market Supplement Policy in use for difficult-to-resource roles. Risk score 16 unmitigated, 12 mitigated.","category":"people","matters":"A lender needs to assess whether the council can maintain service delivery and financial control with stable staffing, and whether pay inflation is sustainable","figures":"4% pay award February 2026; Workforce Strategy reviewed June 2026; risk score 16 unmitigated, 12 mitigated","quote":"Pay award of 4% agreed by Council in February 2026 has helped in ensuring that pay remains competitive with others in the County and therefore score has been reduced.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annex 1a - Strategic Risk Register","paper_url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk/documents/s100364/100364.pdf","headline":"Temporary accommodation costs rising significantly; council deploying \u00a31.6m Local Authority Housing Fund to develop council-owned accommodation portfolio","detail":"Housing need creating sustained increase in temporary accommodation costs. Council received \u00a31.6m Local Authority Housing Fund and is developing council-owned/leased accommodation portfolio, implementing downsizing policy for larger properties, and working with housing providers on homelessness prevention. Homelessness and Rough Sleeping Strategy 2026\u20132031 under development. Risk score 20 unmitigated, 12 mitigated.","category":"demand","matters":"A lender needs to understand whether the council is managing homelessness cost pressures sustainably and whether external funding is being deployed effectively","figures":"\u00a31.6m Local Authority Housing Fund; risk score 20 unmitigated, 12 mitigated","quote":"Development of council owned/leased temporary accommodation portfolio - including delivery of the Local Authority Housing Fund \u00a31.6m funding received.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annex 1a - Strategic Risk Register","paper_url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk/documents/s100364/100364.pdf","headline":"Development Management decisions blocked by insufficient infrastructure capacity \u2014 identified March 2026, unresolved at September review","detail":"The council is unable to make a full range of planning decisions due to evidence of insufficient infrastructure capacity, backing up planning decisions in the system. Statutory provider discussions ongoing. Precautionary approach adopted where all DM decisions reviewed for material considerations. Developers requested to provide individual infrastructure requirements for major applications. Risk score 20 unmitigated, reduced to 8 with mitigation.","category":"capital","matters":"A lender needs to know whether the council can process development and generate planning fees as planned, and whether infrastructure investment is proceeding as required","figures":"Risk identified March 2026; score 20 unmitigated, 8 mitigated","quote":"Being unable to make a full range of Planning decisions due to evidence of insufficient infrastructure capacity would result in planning decisions being held up and backed up in the system.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-03"},"name":"Tonbridge & Malling","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-21","since_iso":"2026-08-22","distress":false,"headline":"Capital expenditure underspent by \u00a31,784k (24%) against budget in 2025/26.","lead":"Material capital underspend indicates the council may not be progressing its capital investment programme as planned, which affects its capacity to deliver improvements and may signal project delivery or prioritization issues.","also":["7 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit Committee on 2026-09-28","n_findings":8,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Annex 4 - TMBC Treasury Management Annual Report 2025/26","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.tmbc.gov.uk/documents/s98947/98947.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":87,"news_drafts_total":1}}